@startuml
title CS-03 / GovernedExecution internal parts\nRefines CS-01 execution : GovernedExecution [1]
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #EEF4F8
skinparam componentBorderColor #27465B
skinparam ArrowColor #27465B
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF5D9
skinparam nodesep 90
skinparam ranksep 60

component "GovernedExecution\n{structured classifier; deterministic}" as Execution {
  portin "work (P)" as EX_WORK
  portin "decisionCheck (P)" as EX_DECISION
  portout "domain (R)" as EX_DOMAIN
  portout "labelStore (R)" as EX_LABELS

  component "operations : OperationsService [1]\n{A2; only operational invoker}" as Ops {
    portin "work (P)" as OP_WORK
    portout "domain (R)" as OP_DOMAIN
    portout "dispatchCheck (R)" as OP_CHECK
    portout "returnsLogistics (R)" as OP_RET
    portout "notification (R)" as OP_NOTIFY
    portout "labelStore (R)" as OP_LABELS
  }
  component "guard : ApprovalGuard [1]\n{A2; verdict is not approval}" as Guard {
    portin "decision (P)" as GU_DECISION
    portin "dispatch (P)" as GU_DISPATCH
  }
  component "returnsLogistics :\nMockReturnsLogisticsAdapter [1]\n{configured provider role; CS-D03}" as ReturnAdapter {
    portin "returnsLogistics (P)" as RE_EFFECT
  }
  component "notification :\nMockNotificationAdapter [1]\n{saved-message delivery only}" as NotifyAdapter {
    portin "notification (P)" as NO_DELIVER
  }
}

EX_WORK -- OP_WORK : D21
EX_DECISION -- GU_DECISION : D22
OP_DOMAIN -- EX_DOMAIN : D23
OP_LABELS -- EX_LABELS : D24
OP_CHECK -- GU_DISPATCH : A21
OP_RET -- RE_EFFECT : A22
OP_NOTIFY -- NO_DELIVER : A23

legend bottom
  A22 new effect requires: current eligible case and PASS/PASS_WITH_WARNING review;
  exact trusted ApprovalRecord; G-DISPATCH + provider permission; durable claim/intent.
  D22 validates the decision before Domain creates approval; A21 rechecks every new effect.
  Operations supplies Domain-loaded records to Guard; Guard has no repository-write port.
  A22 also supports authorised historical lookup; lookup never grants fresh execution authority.
  UNKNOWN is reconciled with original identity before any guarded retry; see MA-0.1.
  A23 needs a saved outcome, not an execution approval: REJECT/manual may notify with zero effects.
  Notification failure cannot replay A22; D23 submits outcomes for Domain to persist and audit.
  Guard/provider observations return through their callers and D23 / D22 to Domain AuditPort.

  P/R = provided/required contract; Dxx delegation; Axx assembly; lines are not message order.
  A22 is a required/provided binding, not permission to bypass A21; preconditions above are mandatory.
  CS-D03: this view is the mock configuration; A3 is a later alternative behind the same port.
  Select exactly one configured adapter per logical operation; no mock + A3 double effect.
  A3 needs separately verified no-charge test authority; no such access is claimed here.
  D24 is A-managed label artifact persistence (CS-Q02), not a customer upload or case-state write.
  MA-D/Q decisions, F.01 acceptance and human review remain pending; no runtime safety proof.
endlegend
@enduml
